# Cursor Rules — Tahawar Ihsan Portfolio v2.0

Read CONTEXT.md for full context. Key rules:

## Stack (don't change)
- Next.js 15 App Router · TypeScript · Tailwind v3.4 · Framer Motion · Geist fonts
- Static export to Netlify (`output: 'export'`)

## Content
- All data in `lib/data.ts`. Edit there, not in components.
- Owner's title is "AI/ML Engineer", never "Software Engineer"
- Public enterprise clients: only BMW and Mercedes
- Never invent metrics

## Design Locks
- Single accent color: electric blue `#3b82f6`. No gradients beyond the subtle hero/contact radial.
- Background: `#0a0a0b`. Sharp corners.
- Geist Sans for body, Geist Mono for technical accents (labels, tags, dates, IDs).
- Don't add purple, no rainbow effects, no neon green.

## SEO Locks
- Don't remove anything from `app/layout.tsx` head: title, description, OG, Twitter, JSON-LD.
- Don't remove `public/robots.txt` or `public/sitemap.xml`.

## Components
- Components using Framer Motion or React hooks must have `'use client'` at the top.
- Match the existing section pattern: number label (mono, accent) → divider → uppercase mono category → section heading → content.

## When asked to add things
- New section: define data type + content in `data.ts`, build a component, add to `app/page.tsx`, add nav entry in `Nav.tsx`, update sitemap.
- New project: add to `projects` array in `data.ts`. UI updates automatically.
- New experience: add to `experience` array in `data.ts`. UI updates automatically.

## Forbidden
- Don't add Google Analytics. Use Plausible or Cloudflare Web Analytics if requested.
- Don't introduce new fonts.
- Don't switch CSS frameworks.
- Don't add a live chatbot demo without explicit approval (API cost + security concerns).
